<%# Layout for :hint-variant responses fetched by the gem's hint
    controller via explicit `hint_url:`. Same wire shape as the
    inline-hint template emitted by `overlay_stack_tag` so the JS
    extractor has one code path: a <template id="…"> wrapping the
    hint chrome partial wrapping the response body.

    Capture yield first (so any `turbo_overlay_hint do … end` block
    in the view has a chance to populate `content_for`), then prefer
    the captured hint over the full page body. This lets a single
    `turbo_overlay_hint` block in `show.html.erb` drive BOTH the
    inline prefetch path AND the explicit `hint_url:` fetch path —
    no need for a separate `show.html+hint.erb` variant just to get
    the same hint body. Apps that want a leaner hint render (skip
    the rest of the view) can still drop a `show.html+hint.erb` that
    returns just the hint body and we'll use yield. %>
<% default_body = capture { yield } %>
<% hint_body = content_for?(:turbo_overlay_hint) ? content_for(:turbo_overlay_hint) : default_body %>
<template id="turbo-overlay-hint"><%= render layout: "turbo_overlay/hint" do %><%= hint_body %><% end %></template>
